## 6. Colour system

### The story

{{COLOUR_STORY}}

### Core (use daily)

| Token | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-bg` | `{{PALETTE_BG}}` | Primary light surface. Default everywhere. |
| `--color-fg` | `{{PALETTE_FG}}` | Primary dark surface + default type colour on light. |
| `--color-accent` | `{{PALETTE_ACCENT}}` | {{SIGNATURE_PRIMITIVE}}. CTAs. **The only saturated colour in the product.** ≤ 8% of any screen. |

### Warm/cool neutrals

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-bg-50` | `{{PALETTE_BG_50}}` | Highest-light surface (cards, inputs) |
| `--color-bg-200` | `{{PALETTE_BG_200}}` | Borders, dividers |
| `--color-bg-300` | `{{PALETTE_BG_300}}` | Muted text on bg |
| `--color-bg-500` | `{{PALETTE_BG_500}}` | Secondary text on bg |
| `--color-fg-300` | `{{PALETTE_FG_300}}` | Hairline on dark |
| `--color-fg-500` | `{{PALETTE_FG_500}}` | Elevated dark surfaces |
| `--color-fg-700` | `{{PALETTE_FG_700}}` | Card bg in dark mode |

### Semantic tokens

Tuned inside the {{PRODUCT}} palette — not bootstrapped from a UI kit.

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-success` | `{{SEMANTIC_SUCCESS}}` | Success states |
| `--color-warning` | `{{SEMANTIC_WARNING}}` | Warnings |
| `--color-danger` | `{{SEMANTIC_DANGER}}` | Destructive / hard-block |
| `--color-info` | `{{SEMANTIC_INFO}}` | Neutral notifications |

### The 62/30/8 rule

Every screen breaks down roughly:

- **~62% bg or fg** (dominant surface)
- **~30% neutrals** (text, borders, secondary surfaces)
- **~8% accent** (CTAs, brand moments, {{SIGNATURE_PRIMITIVE}}s)

When a screen feels "too branded," the accent is over 8%. Pull back.

### Light vs dark — accent is constant

Dark mode swaps bg and fg roles but **keeps the accent identical**. The
brand's only pigment is its only pigment regardless of theme. This is
non-negotiable.

See §17 for the `@theme` + `:root` + `[data-theme="dark"]` implementation.

