## 9. Spacing & layout

### 8-point grid

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--spacing-1` | 4px | Icon gaps, inline micro-spacing |
| `--spacing-2` | 8px | Tight clusters |
| `--spacing-3` | 12px | Form control padding Y |
| `--spacing-4` | 16px | Default gap |
| `--spacing-6` | 24px | Between related blocks |
| `--spacing-8` | 32px | Container padding on desktop |
| `--spacing-12` | 48px | Between sub-sections |
| `--spacing-16` | 64px | Between major sections |
| `--spacing-24` | 96px | Hero padding, page rails |
| `--spacing-32` | 128px | Editorial breathing room |

### Containers

- `--container-max`: 1080px — default
- `--container-narrow`: 680px — long-form copy, legal, onboarding
- `--container-wide`: 1280px — dashboards only

Use logical properties so RTL and notch-safety are automatic:

```css
.rail { padding-inline: max(1rem, env(safe-area-inset-left)); }
```

### Radii

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--radius-sm` | 6px | Inputs, badges |
| `--radius-md` | 10px | Dropdowns, chips |
| `--radius-lg` | 14px | Cards, modals |
| `--radius-xl` | 20px | Feature panels |
| `--radius-pill` | 9999px | Buttons, pills |

**Concentric radii rule**: nested elements share curvature. A `--radius-lg`
card holds children with `--radius-md`. Never mix arbitrary radii inside
one composition.

### Density — marketing vs dashboard

Marketing pages use `--spacing-16` to `--spacing-32` between major
blocks. Dashboards halve this. Tight is what everyone else does —
marketing goes the other way.

