## 11. Motion

### Principle

**Static by default.** Motion serves two jobs only: confirming a user
action (150–250ms), or embodying the signature primitive. Everything
else is off.

### Tokens

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--ease-out` | `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` | Enters, hovers |
| `--ease-in-out` | `cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1)` | Bi-directional |
| `--duration-fast` | 150ms | Hover, focus, small state changes |
| `--duration-base` | 200ms | Dropdowns, tooltips |
| `--duration-slow` | 320ms | Modals, sheets |

### The signature animation

```css
@keyframes signature-pulse {
  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1);    opacity: 1; }
  50%      { transform: scale(0.92); opacity: 0.85; }
}
.{{SIGNATURE_PRIMITIVE_CLASS}} { animation: signature-pulse 1.8s var(--ease-in-out) infinite; }
```

### Reduced motion

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

