## 14. Accessibility

### Contrast floors — WCAG 2.2 AA

- **Body text**: 4.5:1
- **Large text** (≥ 24px, or ≥ 19px bold): 3:1
- **UI controls, focus rings, non-text**: 3:1
- **Target size** (WCAG 2.2 new AA, 2.5.8): ≥ 24×24 CSS px, with exceptions for inline text links

{{CONTRAST_MATRIX}}

Run `~/.claude/skills/brand-system/scripts/audit-contrast.py \
  --bg {{PALETTE_BG}} --fg {{PALETTE_FG}} --accent {{PALETTE_ACCENT}}`
to refresh.

### Focus rings

```css
:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
  border-radius: inherit;
}
```

New in WCAG 2.2 (2.4.11 **Focus Not Obscured**): the focus ring cannot
be fully hidden behind a sticky header, toast, or overlay. Audit with
keyboard-only navigation.

### Reduced motion

See §11. All motion respects `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

### Forced colors (Windows high-contrast)

```css
@media (forced-colors: active) {
  :root { --accent: CanvasText; --border: CanvasText; }
}
```

### RTL equivalence

Every feature works identically in RTL and LTR. Never ship a feature
QA'd only in one direction. Logical CSS properties
(`padding-inline-start`, `margin-block-end`) everywhere. Never
`padding-left`.

